"use strict";(self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc=self.webpackChunkwp_woocommerce_pre_order_doc||[]).push([[414],{1428(e,r,t){t.r(r),t.d(r,{_pageData:()=>a,default:()=>s});var o=t(641);const a=JSON.parse('{"path":"/woocommerce-pre-order/order-cancellation.html","title":"Pre-Order Cancellation Management","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"woocommerce-pre-order/order-cancellation.md"}'),n={name:"order-cancellation.md"},s=(0,t(6262).A)(n,[["render",function(e,r,t,a,n,s){return(0,o.uX)(),(0,o.CE)("div",null,[...r[0]||(r[0]=[(0,o.Fv)('<h1 id="pre-order-cancellation-management" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#pre-order-cancellation-management"><span>Pre-Order Cancellation Management</span></a></h1><p>The WooCommerce Pre-Order plugin provides a complete, merchant-friendly <strong>Pre-Order Cancellation Request workflow</strong>. This system allows customers to request cancellations directly from their account dashboards while giving administrators full control to review, approve, automatically refund, or decline cancellation requests.</p><hr><h2 id="_1-the-cancellation-request-workflow" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-the-cancellation-request-workflow"><span>1. The Cancellation Request Workflow</span></a></h2><p>Below is the visual workflow detailing how a customer cancellation request is routed and processed:</p><hr><h2 id="_2-administrator-settings-days-to-cancel" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-administrator-settings-days-to-cancel"><span>2. Administrator Settings (Days to Cancel)</span></a></h2><p>Administrators can control which pre-orders are eligible for customer cancellation. Go to <strong>WooCommerce</strong> &gt; <strong>Pre-Order List</strong> &gt; <strong>Configuration</strong> &gt; <strong>Days to Cancel</strong> tab to define the cancellation window:</p><ul><li><strong>Cancel Status:</strong> Toggle to enable or disable customer-initiated pre-order cancellation requests globally.</li><li><strong>Cancel Before (Days):</strong> Enter the number of days before the product release date during which the customer can submit a cancellation request. If left empty or set to <code>0</code>, the customer can request cancellation anytime up until the actual release.</li></ul><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/admin-days-to-cancel.png" alt="Days to Cancel Configuration Settings"></p><hr><h2 id="_3-customer-cancellation-request-flow-storefront" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-customer-cancellation-request-flow-storefront"><span>3. Customer Cancellation Request Flow (Storefront)</span></a></h2><p>Registered and guest customers can request cancellation from their respective pre-order lists:</p><ol><li><p><strong>Locate Pre-Order:</strong> Navigate to <strong>My Account</strong> &gt; <strong>Pre-Orders</strong> (registered customers) or the <strong>My Pre-Orders</strong> OTP portal (guests).</p></li><li><p><strong>Submit Request:</strong> In the pre-order table, click the <strong>Cancel Pre-Order</strong> button under the actions column.</p><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/customer-my-preorders.png" alt="Customer Dashboard showing Pre-Orders"></p></li><li><p><strong>Provide Reason:</strong> A secure modal will appear. Enter a brief reason for requesting the cancellation, then click <strong>Submit Request</strong>.</p><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/front-end-cancellation-modal.png" alt="Cancel Pre-Order Request Modal"></p></li><li><p><strong>Pending Status:</strong> The customer&#39;s dashboard updates immediately to show a notice that the cancellation request has been submitted for review.</p><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/customer-my-preorders-cancellation-submitted.png" alt="Cancellation Request Submitted Confirmation"></p></li></ol><hr><h2 id="_4-processing-requests-admin-dashboard" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-processing-requests-admin-dashboard"><span>4. Processing Requests (Admin Dashboard)</span></a></h2><p>Store administrators manage incoming cancellation requests under <strong>WooCommerce</strong> &gt; <strong>Pre-Order List</strong> &gt; <strong>Cancellation Requests</strong>:</p><h3 id="the-cancellation-requests-list" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#the-cancellation-requests-list"><span>The Cancellation Requests List</span></a></h3><p>The dashboard table displays all pending, approved, and declined requests with their associated order numbers, product names, customer details, submission date, and status.</p><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/admin-cancellation-requests-list.png" alt="Admin Cancellation Requests Dashboard"></p><h3 id="reviewing-a-request" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#reviewing-a-request"><span>Reviewing a Request</span></a></h3><p>To action a pending request, click the <strong>Review</strong> button under the order row. This displays a detailed audit screen including the customer&#39;s specified cancellation reason, original order totals, and refundable amount.</p><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/admin-cancellation-request-review.png" alt="Reviewing Cancellation Details"></p><h3 id="approving-a-cancellation-and-refund" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#approving-a-cancellation-and-refund"><span>Approving a Cancellation and Refund</span></a></h3><ol><li>On the review screen, click <strong>Approve &amp; Refund</strong>.</li><li>A confirmation dialog will appear. Optionally enter a private refund note to attach to the WooCommerce order, then click <strong>Approve &amp; Refund</strong>.</li><li>The system automatically cancels the pre-order and triggers a standard refund process for the pre-order deposit or full price paid.</li></ol><p><img src="/woocommerce-pre-order/images/woocommerce-pre-order/admin-cancellation-approve-modal.png" alt="Confirming Approval and Refund"></p><h3 id="declining-a-request" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#declining-a-request"><span>Declining a Request</span></a></h3><ol><li>Click the <strong>Decline Request</strong> button on the review screen.</li><li>Provide a reason for the decline (e.g., &quot;Cancellation request submitted past the allowed window&quot;).</li><li>Click <strong>Decline Request</strong>. The pre-order remains active, and the customer receives an automated email notification with your reason.</li></ol><blockquote><p>[!NOTE] Automated refunds rely on the payment gateway used during the original checkout. For offline or check payments, the store admin must issue refunds manually, while the pre-order status will still update to &quot;Cancelled&quot; in the database.</p></blockquote>',29)])])}]])}}]);